    <string name="eth_speed_title">Link speed</string>
    <string name="eth_speed_value" formatted="false">100 Mbps negotiated \u00b7 about 3 Mbps measured</string>
    <string name="eth_speed_note_title">Why only about 3 Mbps?</string>
    <string name="eth_speed_note" formatted="false">The wired NIC is a WIZnet W5500, an SPI-attached Ethernet controller. Its PHY supports 10/100 Mbps, but SPI transactions plus driver overhead cost roughly 5 ms per packet, capping throughput at about 3 Mbps (\u2248375 KB/s) in both directions. This is a hardware limitation that no system setting can improve \u2014 use Wi-Fi when you need real speed.</string>

